# Plan part F10 (proposed ADR-0443, INV-0443-5; ADR-0262: what is made for a client is paid
# by the client): the image of a program the shell starts in a room is charged to the room's
# job. `t_unix` is a 1.1 MiB program. A room at 1M cannot start it: the shell says "over quota"
# at the image, twice, and the room's row (`top tight`) reads the same before, between and
# after (tools/check-room-image.py); a room at 64M starts the same program. A refusal at the
# image leaves nothing in the room: no process, no image, no handle.
! panicked
! ZORAYA-PANIC
< \r\n~> 
> room new tight --mem 1M --procs 16 +w /work\r
< tight --colour
< \r\n~> 
> room new roomy --mem 64M --procs 16 +w /work\r
< roomy --colour
< \r\n~> 
> room tight\r
< tight /work> 
> top tight\r
< limits --mem 1M
< tight /work> 
> /bin/t_unix pair\r
< over quota
< tight /work> 
> top tight\r
< limits --mem 1M
< tight /work> 
> /bin/t_unix pair\r
< over quota
< tight /work> 
> top tight\r
< limits --mem 1M
< tight /work> 
> top tight\r
< limits --mem 1M
< tight /work> 
> room --leave\r
< \r\n/work> 
> room roomy\r
< roomy /work> 
> /bin/t_unix pair\r
< t_unix: pair passed
< roomy /work> 
> room --leave\r
< \r\n/work> 
> room remove tight --kill\r
< \r\n/work> 
> room remove roomy --kill\r
< \r\n/work> 
> poweroff\r
